    "narrative": "For LawDog today, our offensive ceiling is anchored by the favorable matchup against Fedde, pushing **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) to the top of our lineup. Both players benefit significantly from the +16% park factor and the +19% SP skill boost provided by Fedde\u2019s projected struggles. **Taylor Ward** serves as our primary engine despite a slight platoon drag, while **Dylan Beavers** occupies the high-leverage #3 spot, making him arguably our most explosive asset. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** (64.99) and **Bryson Stott** (65.58) provide elite efficiency; **Luis Arraez**\u2019s +10% order bonus leading off against Pfaadt is a massive stabilizer, and **Bryson Stott** finds himself in a high-scoring spot against Chandler, where his favorable platoon split (+13%) compensates for the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Daulton Varsho**, who finished with a 49.53 score, effectively ending up on the outside looking in. While his +10% platoon edge against McLean was enticing, the -17% penalty for the opposing starter\u2019s skill set suppressed his output just enough to keep him behind the more efficient profiles of **Masyn Winn** and **Drew Gilbert**. We are managing our game caps carefully, and **Yainer Diaz** (38.98) fell well below our threshold, confirming his spot on the bench. As we look at the slate, monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** (53.51); while he is active, his matchup against Soriano is neutral at best, and we are proceeding without the production of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, who remain sidelined on the IL. With no major weather concerns currently flagged, our focus remains on maximizing speed in this high-scoring environment to address our scarcity in the stolen base category.",
